<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>Resume – Example Profile</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

  <style>
    :root{
      --border:#111;
      --muted:#555;
      --accent:#0b5fff;
    }
    *{box-sizing:border-box}
    body{
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      background:#f7f7f7;
      margin:24px;
      display:flex; 
      justify-content:center;
    }
    .resume{
      background:#fff;
      border:2px solid var(--border);
      width: 760px;
      max-width: 100%;
      padding:22px 26px 28px;
    }
    .top{
      display:flex;
      gap:22px;
      align-items:flex-start;
      margin-bottom:18px;
    }
    .photo{
      width:120px; height:120px;
      border:2px solid var(--border);
      overflow:hidden; 
      flex:0 0 120px;
      background:#eee;
    }
    .photo img{
      width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover;
      display:block;
    }
    .heading h1{
      margin:0 0 6px 0; font-size:24px; letter-spacing:.5px;
    }
    .heading .label{ color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:6px; }
    .heading .name{ font-weight:700; }
    .heading .email a{ color:var(--accent); text-decoration:none; }
    h3{
        margin:18px 0 8px; font-size:18px;
      border-bottom:1px solid #ddd; padding-bottom:4px;
    }
    p{ margin:8px 0; line-height:1.45; }
    ul{ margin:6px 0 8px 20px; }
    .projects{
      display:flex; gap:14px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:6px;
    }
    .project-box{
      border:2px solid var(--border);
      padding:10px 12px; width:320px; background:#fafafa;
    }
    .project-box h4{ margin:0 0 6px; }
    .two-col{
      display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap:14px;
    }
    .small{ color:var(--muted); font-size:13px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <main class="resume">
    <!-- Top: Photo + Headings -->
    <section class="top">
      <div class="photo">
        <!-- /home/labuser/Desktop/web development/photo-1599508704512-2f19efd1e35f.avif-->
        <img src="images/myphoto.jpg" alt="Profile photo">
      </div>

      <div class="heading">
        <div class="label">RESUME</div>
        <h1 class="name">Chethan Venkatesh</h1>
        <div class="email">Email: <a href="mailto:chethan@example.com">chethan@example.com</a></div>
        <div class="small">Phone: +91-98765-43210 · Bengaluru</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Objective (≈100 words) -->
    <h3>Objective</h3>
    <p>
      Aspiring software developer and current apprentice with a strong interest in building clean, reliable applications. 
      I aim to contribute to real-world projects where I can apply core Java, data structures, and web fundamentals while 
      learning production practices such as version control, unit testing, and debugging. I value simple design, readable 
      code, and collaborative teamwork. Over the next year, my goal is to deepen my understanding of problem solving, 
      algorithms, and API integration, and to deliver features that improve user experience and performance in measurable ways.
    </p>
    <!-- Marks -->
    <h3>Marks</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>10th Board – 88%</li>
      <li>12th Board – 86%</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- Technologies -->
    <h3>Technologies</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Java, OOP, Collections (ArrayList, LinkedList, HashMap)</li>
      <li>HTML, CSS, Basic JavaScript · Git & GitHub · Eclipse/VS Code</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- About You (≈200 words) -->
    <h3>About You</h3>
    <p>
      I am a detail-oriented learner who enjoys understanding how systems work from the ground up. 
      During my apprenticeship, I have practiced writing modular Java programs, handling exceptions, 
      and organizing code into packages to keep responsibilities clear. I like to break problems into 
      small steps, write simple tests, and iterate until the solution is robust. When I get stuck, I 
      read documentation, search for minimal examples, and ask focused questions. Outside pure coding, 
      I care about communication and sharing findings with teammates through short notes or demos.
    </p>
    <p>
      Recently, I have experimented with building basic web pages and connecting them to Java backends. 
      I am comfortable using Git branches, logging meaningful messages, and reviewing pull requests. 
      My immediate focus areas are improving algorithmic thinking, writing cleaner unit tests with JUnit, 
      and learning how to read unfamiliar codebases quickly. I am motivated by mentorship, constructive feedback, 
      and opportunities to turn specifications into working features that customers actually use.
    </p>

    <!-- Projects (two DIV elements) -->
    <h3>Projects</h3>
    <div class="projects">
      <div class="project-box">
        <h4>1st project – Banking Console App</h4>
        <p class="small">Java · Custom exceptions · Collections</p>
        <p>
          Built a small console application to simulate accounts, deposits, withdrawals, and transfers. 
          Implemented custom exceptions for low balance and invalid operations; stored users in a HashMap 
          and transactions in an ArrayList.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-box">
        <h4>2nd project – Student Records Manager</h4>
        <p class="small">Java · File I/O · Sorting & Filtering</p>
        <p>
          Designed a CLI to add, update, and list students with marks. 
          Implemented sorting by total and filtering by subject; persisted data to CSV and loaded on startup.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Personal Details -->
    <h3>Personal Details</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>DOB: 15-08-2004</li>
      <li>City: Bengaluru</li>
    </ul>
  </main>

</body>
</html>
